&lt;p&gt;Join us for a thought-provoking panel discussion featuring four distinguished leaders at the forefront of healthcare innovation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Laurent Ganem &amp;#39;86&lt;/strong&gt;, Founder and Chief Executive Officer, G Square Healthcare Private Equity LLP,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Junaid Bajwa&lt;/strong&gt;, Operating Partner, G Square Healthcare Private Equity,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Lewis Potter&lt;/strong&gt;, NHS Clinical Entrepreneur, Founder and CEO, Geeky Medics, and&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Tim Crimmins&lt;/strong&gt;,&amp;nbsp;Chief Medical Information Officer, Columbia University Irving Medical Center, will delve into the evolving landscape of AI in healthcare. The panelists will explore themes such as the future of AI investments in healthcare, enhanced training for clinicians using AI tools, and the deployment and potential of AI within the healthcare industry. The conversation will explore emerging trends in healthcare, including ethical and practical considerations shaping innovation. The panel will be moderated by Professor Carri Chan,&amp;nbsp;Cain Brothers and Company Professor of Healthcare Management and Faculty Director, Healthcare and Pharmaceutical Management Program.&lt;/p&gt;
